Final Thought
The engineers who stand out in Kafka interviews aren’t the ones who memorize definitions — they’re the ones who can say:

“We had 50k messages piling up in production. I checked the consumer group lag, found one partition was 10x slower than others, traced it to a hot key causing uneven distribution, and fixed it by switching to a composite key.”

Build that vocabulary. Run Kafka locally. Break things intentionally. Read the server.properties docs. That's what separates a Kafka user from a Kafka engineer.
